{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nThe prior slices establish a bounded structural index and Terraform-only tool sessions in both review pipelines [rebar:depraved-classless-rooster]. This slice adds optional independent corroboration from HashiCorp's `terraform-config-inspect` when it is already on `PATH`. Audited basis: commit `2fb54c236733ee65ee877105d595c124c993c64d`, whose shallow loader extracts top-level metadata with a nil expression context and runs no Terraform.\n\n## Scope\n\nAdd `src/rebar/grounding/terraform_corroborator.py` and expose `corroborate_diagnostic(module, diagnostic, subject, expected=None)` through established Terraform Pass-1 and Pass-2 sessions.\n\n### Closed query and result contract\n\nAccepted diagnostics are:\n\n- `declaration_present`: named variable, output, managed resource, data resource, module call, or required provider.\n- `module_source_equals`: a named module call has the normalized expected literal source.\n- `required_provider_present`: a named provider requirement exists.\n\nAn exact schema-valid entry returns `match` at T1. Missing or unequal entries, absence claims, and unsupported/computed semantics return `abstain`; upstream silence never proves correctness or absence. Results contain only normalized names, classes, positions, and hashes—not descriptions, defaults, constraints, diagnostics, or other upstream literal payloads. The closed receipt schema is extended to represent this operation: `corroborate_diagnostic` joins the `operation` enum and `match` joins the `outcome` enum, guarded so only the corroborator may emit `match` (the refutation-only ops stay `refuted`/`abstain`); the receipt records the corroborator's operation, outcome, and result digest.\n\n### Hardened execution\n\n- Resolve only the exact `terraform-config-inspect` basename from inherited `PATH`; canonicalize once and reject non-regular/non-executable or repo/snapshot-contained candidates. Invoke its absolute path without a shell using only `--json <snapshot>`; never pass `--after-init`, `--stack`, repository arguments, or shell text.\n- Copy the immutable indexed whole-module bytes into a fresh directory: regular `.tf` and `.tf.json` files only, no symlinks. Make it read-only, run there, and never pass the repository path.\n- Close stdin, create a process group/session, and allow only locale, OS-required process variables, and temporary `HOME`/`TMPDIR`. Strip Terraform/OpenTofu, provider/cloud credential, proxy, plugin, CLI-config, and repository variables.\n- Apply the existing 60-second deadline; cap stdout at 4 MiB and stderr at 64 KiB. On timeout, overflow, cancellation, or error, terminate then kill and reap the whole group and remove the snapshot. Hash the executable before and after; replacement abstains.\n- Record backend, canonical path, SHA-256, discoverable version or `unknown`, invocation profile, snapshot digest, normalized query, outcome, and result digest. Never log child streams or environment values.\n\nValidate stdout against a Rebar-owned schema for the audited JSON fields; every reported filename must name a copied snapshot file. Unknown/malformed shapes, upstream diagnostics, nonzero exit, overflow, path mismatch, binary replacement, or schema skew (upstream JSON failing that schema — a field renamed/removed/reshaped versus the pinned `2fb54c23`) produce one closed abstention with no partial facts. A `match` is gated on schema validity, never the version string: the version is provenance-only and the binary is pinned by SHA-256 (hashed before/after). A corroborator can strengthen a positive Pass-1 fact or independently support Pass-2; it cannot originate a finding, veto ordinary review, or turn abstention into negative evidence.\n\n### Pinned upstream canary\n\nExtend the optionality workflow with a gating lane that installs the pinned `terraform-config-inspect@2fb54c23…` commit, exposes only that binary on the test `PATH`, and drives the real adapter over a module containing every supported declaration. Assert positive matches, absence-as-abstention, schema acceptance, provenance, and cleanup. Normal unit tests remain network-free and substitute an executable fixture only at the process boundary.\n\n## Positive rationale\n\nHashiCorp's deliberately shallow extractor is a narrow authoritative cross-check; the minimal snapshot and fixed process contract keep repository config, plugins, cached modules, and ambient credentials from affecting it, and match-only semantics absorb upstream incompleteness safely.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nTerraform/OpenTofu and provider execution; validate/plan/init/get; TFLint, Trivy, tfparse, terraform-ls, terraform-docs; module fetch; after-init/stack modes; arbitrary diagnostics; absence claims; expression evaluation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Unit tests through the production adapter prove the closed diagnostic enum and exact-match T1 outcomes for every supported class; missing, unequal, absence-claim, and computed controls return `abstain`.\n- [ ] Parent/child subprocess tests capture argv, cwd, stdin, environment, permissions, and bytes, proving only canonical `terraform-config-inspect --json <snapshot>` launches and no repo path, symlink, credential/config variable, or forbidden executable reaches it.\n- [ ] Timeout, overflow, cancellation, nonzero-exit, and parser-failure fault tests observe process-group reaping and snapshot removal before return; a clean retry succeeds.\n- [ ] Producer/consumer contract tests prove diagnostics, unknown/malformed fields, escaping filenames, changed binary digests, and version/schema skew yield one redacted abstention without partial facts.\n- [ ] Receipt tests assert provenance fields and byte-scan results, receipts, logs, and exceptions to prove fixture literals, credentials, streams, and environment values never escape.\n- [ ] Terraform plan-review and code-review Pass 1/Pass 2 advertise `corroborate_diagnostic`; non-IaC and missing-extra sessions do not, and abstention leaves the ordinary decision path unchanged.\n- [ ] The optionality workflow runs the real adapter against the exact audited commit and fails on drift; `docs/grounding.md` gives the same opt-in local canary.\n- [ ] ADR 0115 (the established Terraform structural-grounding ADR, already amended by 1c52) gains a new section recording the `terraform-config-inspect` executable trust boundary, audited commit, match-only semantics, and the standing prohibition on every other Terraform-related executable. No new ADR number is allocated (0111 and 0116 are taken by unrelated Accepted ADRs).\n\n## Testing\n\nTest contract card:\n\n- Contract: REB-640, upstream README/JSON at the pinned commit, [rebar:depraved-classless-rooster].\n- Preconditions: indexed module; executable fixtures for success, skew, secret-bearing output, overflow, hang, signal-resistant child, self-replacement; pinned real binary in the canary.\n- Production path: real snapshot, discovery, launcher, bounded capture, schema parser, receipt, routing; unit tests replace only the executable.\n- Tiers: schema unit, real parent/child subprocess, workflow integration, live upstream canary.\n- Oracles: exact outcome/tier/reason; captured child contract; child absent + snapshot removed + retry OK; exact receipt; byte-level non-disclosure.\n- Negative controls: exact positive matches, nearest absence/inequality abstains, non-Terraform routes expose no tool.\n- CI: `make test` plus the gating pinned-upstream optionality canary.\n\n## Verification\n\n`env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_corroborator.py tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_code_review_tools.py`\n\nAC7/AC8 pinned-upstream canary (gating; identical opt-in command in `docs/grounding.md`):\n\n`go install github.com/hashicorp/terraform-config-inspect@2fb54c236733ee65ee877105d595c124c993c64d && env PATH=\"$(go env GOPATH)/bin:$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" REBAR_TERRAFORM_CONFIG_INSPECT_CANARY=1 python -m pytest tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_corroborator.py -k pinned_upstream_canary`"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788585787242611001,"uuid":"0ff77dcd-7e81-4cd5-aab2-7030e6a53f70"}